From c9c7080efcd2a44a906222ba0091c227a9eb1844 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: hiper25 <whydonit@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 07:17:49 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] clk: meson: Program SC2 secure PLL output rates atomically

SC2 firmware programs M, N and OD from a final output-frequency request.
Treating the secure service as a DCO writer lets CCF split that operation
and sends the wrong rate. A parked-CPU experiment reproduced the fault;
only the original output-rate request restored the PLL configuration.

Implement SC2-specific SYS and GP1 output operations with BSP rate tables,
lock polling and hardware output verification. Keep their published DCO
clocks read-only and read the actual DCO when recalculating output rates,
rather than using a cache made stale by firmware. Remove the obsolete
secure DCO writer without changing ordinary Meson PLL programming.


---
 drivers/clk/meson/clk-pll.c    | 121 ---------------------
 drivers/clk/meson/clk-secure.h |   1 -
 drivers/clk/meson/sc2.c        | 192 ++++++++++++++++++++++++---------
 3 files changed, 144 insertions(+), 170 deletions(-)

